In article <91Mar1.102038est.2159@ois.db.toronto.edu> jdd@db.toronto.edu (John DiMarco) writes:
>One more problem with Nethack: the ring of conflict is a little too 
>powerful. 

I agree.


>It may be a good idea to limit the range of a ring of conflict to 2 or 3
>squares. i.e. if a monster is farther than 2 or 3 squares from a player, it
>isn't affected.  
>

UNfortunately if you did this, it wouldn't matter, all you would have to
do is wait for the monsters in a 2-3 square area to kill each other, and
then let the other monsters get within range.  It would take longer to
kill all of the monsters, but this would make it no more difficult.

Maybe you could make it cause only certain classes to fight each other,
like monsters of opposite alignment would fight each other.  Maybe
neutrals aren't affected?  Or maybe monsters of your OWN alignment would
fight monsters of other alignments.

Just a couple of suggestions.

>John

